 Shuttle Bus Schedules [pdf] Resources Division of Student Development Student Handbook (policies and resources) University Bookstore Other Departments Website Comments Equity & Inclusion Division of Equity and Inclusion Office for Student Diversity and Inclusion Services Accessibility Resource Center (Disability Services) Career Development Child Development Center Dean of Students Events and Conference Services Student Accounts (Bursar) Student Enrollment Services Veteran/Military Services Health & Safety University Police Rave Guardian Mobile App Counseling, Health, & Wellness Center Safe Walk Escort Service About Us What's Happening University News Events Calendar Arts on Campus Social Media Directory Community Child Development Center Civic Engagement Consumer Information Employment Opportunities Hispanic-Serving Institution Our Community University Police University Sustainability About WP All Departments University Facts Our History Our Background Mission, Vision, and Core Values Honors and Awards University Annual Report Student Achievements University Virtual Tour Our Alumni Giving to WP University Policies Open Public Records Request Strategic Plan Equity & Inclusion Division of Equity and Inclusion Office for Student Diversity and Inclusion Administration Board of Trustees Office of the President Provost and Academic Affairs Administration, Capital Planning, and Physical Plant Operations Enrollment Management Equity and Inclusion Finance and Controller General Counsel Human Resources Information Technology Institutional Advancement Marketing and Public Relations Strategic Initiatives and University Relations Student Development Athletics Cultural Events WP connect Maps & Contact Give Apply INFORMATION FOR Prospective Students Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Family Donors Alumni Our Local Community Human Resources Human Resources Home Jobs/Careers/Compensation Employment Opportunities Professional and Organizational Development Career Path Options Compensation and Classification Salary Range and Step Information Job Descriptions Position Classification and Reclassification Workweek Definitions and Overtime Eligibility Recruitment Total Rewards Institutional Equity and Diversity Ethics and Compliance Policies, Forms, Contracts Calendar Schedule Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Announcements Human Resources Staff OneHR Customer Service Center Compensation and Classification William Paterson University views compensation as the entirety of monetary and non-monetary benefits provided to our workforce as a critical factor in our ability to attract, retain, reward, and recognize our diverse workforce of qualified employees. Compensation (pay) for unionized positions is governed by contractually negotiated agreements between the State of New Jersey and the respective bargaining unit. For managerial and other positions not covered by a bargaining unit (non-aligned), the University strives to ensure that employees performing the same work, with same or similar skill level, competencies, experience, education, training, and professional credentials are compensated equitably while allowing flexibility driven by strategic initiative and the financial health of the University. Positions at William Paterson University fall into two categories: Unclassified and Classified/Career Service. Unclassified (exempt from NJ Civil Service) positions are generally executives, managers, and professional administrative staff who are exempt from the minimum wage and overtime provisions of the Fair Labor Standards Act. This category includes faculty, librarians, AFT professional staff, higher education managers and confidential non-aligned employees. Classified /Career Service positions are generally subject to the minimum wage and overtime provisions of the Fair Labor Standards Act. Additionally, hiring, evaluation, promotion and discipline processes are governed by the rules and regulations of the Civil Service Commission (CSC) and applicable collective bargaining agreements between the State of New Jersey and the respective unions which represent these employees. Positions in this category are typically administrative and technical support, computing technology, facilities maintenance trades, custodial, and public safety. Request Info Visit Apply Quick Links Employment Opportunities Campus Map Contact Us Get Connected Event Calendar WP News Give to William Paterson Social Media Directory WP Connect 300 Pompton Road | Wayne, New Jersey 07470 (973) 720-2000 Copyright © 2026 | Privacy Policy"
    },
